From 875e35e6ec5df9ed52db109953db2288e7d8cfa8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caleb Jones <caleb@calebgj.io>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:25:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] arch, vmm: riscv64: Describe guest NUMA nodes in the FDT

--numa was accepted on riscv64 but never reached the guest: the VM
dropped the NUMA nodes and the guest kernel faked a single node.

Keep the NUMA nodes on riscv64 and describe them in the FDT following
the devicetree NUMA binding, like aarch64 does: "numa-node-id" on the
CPU nodes, on one memory node per NUMA node and on the PCI host
bridges of the segments assigned to a node, plus a
"numa-distance-map-v1" distance map.

Unlike aarch64, memory zones that are not part of any NUMA node are
still described (without a node id) instead of being left out of the
guest's memory map. Distances only configured in one direction are
used for both.

Signed-off-by: Caleb Jones <caleb@calebgj.io>
